From e3358f5e74f6f31d3dc35b9045d98c3379836f94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:14:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 078/115] ASoC: q6afe: fix the inverted I2S word-clock source

q6afe_i2s_port_prepare() maps the DAI clock-provider format onto the AFE
port's ws_src field, and the two cases are the wrong way round.

SND_SOC_DAIFMT_ names describe the CODEC's role, so BC_FC -- codec bit-
and frame-clock consumer, the old CBS_CFS -- is the configuration in
which the SoC is the master and the LPASS has to generate the word clock
itself, i.e. ws_src INTERNAL. The code asks for an external word clock
there instead, and for an internal one in BP_FP where the codec drives
it. The mapping predates the CBS_CFS -> BC_FC rename, which swapped the
meaning of the labels without swapping the bodies.

Any board with a q6afe MI2S backend and a clock-consumer codec is
affected. Measured on a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, TAS2557 amplifiers on
Quaternary MI2S, SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC): with the old mapping the bit
clock ran but the WS pad stayed parked high for the whole stream, so the
amplifiers never saw a frame and playback was silent.

Fixes: 1148e16b335f ("ASoC: qcom: Update to use set_fmt_new callback")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
index 7b59d514b432..bca5bc3b667d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -1514,11 +1514,17 @@ int q6afe_i2s_port_prepare(struct q6afe_port *port, struct q6afe_i2s_cfg *cfg)
 	pcfg->i2s_cfg.bit_width = cfg->bit_width;
 	pcfg->i2s_cfg.data_format = AFE_LINEAR_PCM_DATA;
 
+	/*
+	 * The clock-provider names are written from the codec's point of view,
+	 * so BC_FC (codec bit- and frame-clock consumer) is the case where the
+	 * CPU has to generate the word clock itself.
+	 */
 	switch (cfg->fmt & SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CLOCK_PROVIDER_MASK) {
-	case SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BP_FP:
+	case SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BC_FC:
+		/* CPU is master */
 		pcfg->i2s_cfg.ws_src = AFE_PORT_CONFIG_I2S_WS_SRC_INTERNAL;
 		break;
-	case SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BC_FC:
+	case SND_SOC_DAIFMT_BP_FP:
 		/* CPU is slave */
 		pcfg->i2s_cfg.ws_src = AFE_PORT_CONFIG_I2S_WS_SRC_EXTERNAL;
 		break;
